      "body": [
        {
          "type": "TextualBody",
          "label": "Recto",
          "value": "\n<ol><li>. . . One thing I have asked</li>\n<li>of the Lord, that will I seek after (Ps. 24:7). Do not turn away the oppressed shamefaced.</li>\n<li>I desire you to advise me on what I propose to do&mdash;namely</li>\n<li>to eat the amount which you have prescribed, but to diminish it daily</li>\n<li>by about a dirham, according to what seems to you beneficial, and</li>\n<li>stop with this at a level which you order to me; since my entire aim</li>\n<li>in this matter is to get near to Him with all my force (or: spirit). Do not neglect me</li>\n<li>regarding what you can do in this matter, for the sake of God, since I have seen in</li>\n<li>the book of al-Fawwal that if the stomach is refined. . .</li>\n<li>the blood, there rises from it a fine steam which becomes what is called</li>\n<li>spirit, and according to the purity of this spirit and the degree of clarity in its organs,</li>\n<li>the faculties of the soul arise from it, and it [the soul] is prepared to receive its influences.</li>\n<li>Prescribe to me what I should cook if occasion sometimes arises: something</li>\n<li>which agrees with this aim, but is not expensive. Judge me leniently</li>\n<li>for these words, according to my ignorance. May your peace increase, amen selah.</li></ol>\n",
          "format": "text/html"
        }
      ],
      "motivation": [
        "sc:supplementing",
        "translating"
      ],
